    "q-103830": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103830",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$\n\nI. The function has a vertical asymptote at $x=11\\pi .$\n\nII. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nIII. $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a root of the function.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264109/assets/7785ad73f6e5212772c3053780ffd055f37cfb39927b6ddc3e40cd3a55b8ba4e.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The vertical asymptotes of the function are at integer multiples of $\\pi $, i.e., $x=n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is any integer.\n\n- Statement II is true. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n.$ Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a root of the function.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
