    "q-103838": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103838",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-4$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+17\\pi )+6.$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=17$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+17\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+17\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-4,$ then $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+17\\pi )=-4.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+7\\pi )+6 & =3(-4)+6 \\\\  & =-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
