    "q-158055": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158055",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{5}{2},$ then $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(-x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264109/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(-x) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
